00:14:15,820 --> 00:14:20,577
I don't hear anything.

258
00:14:20,660 --> 00:14:23,020
You liar, he's right there!

259
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,500
You're serious, aren't you?

260
00:14:26,680 --> 00:14:31,420
I can't believe this You're really
gonna leave without me, huh?

261
00:14:38,160 --> 00:14:39,277
That's fine.

262
00:14:39,360 --> 00:14:40,889
You've made your decision.

263
00:14:41,120 --> 00:14:45,140
If that's how it is, then I have
only one thing to say to you.

264
00:14:45,380 --> 00:14:47,840
Wherever I go, it's my business.

265
00:14:48,240 --> 00:14:50,475
It has nothing to do with you anymore.

266
00:14:53,320 --> 00:14:54,640
I'm leaving the crew.

267
00:14:55,020 --> 00:14:56,480
This is goodbyes.

268
00:15:07,700 --> 00:15:09,597
I'm too stubborn! I know!

269
00:15:09,680 --> 00:15:12,160
I take back every word I said!

270
00:15:22,960 --> 00:15:24,220
That's more like it.

271
00:15:27,540 --> 00:15:29,640
I know I'm being pathetic.

272
00:15:30,080 --> 00:15:32,180
I know I already said I quit.

273
00:15:34,800 --> 00:15:38,017
But will you let me take it back please

274
00:15:38,100 --> 00:15:42,920
I'm begging you you gotta forgive me!

275
00:15:46,140 --> 00:15:52,440
If I'm not with you there's no point
don't leave me alone I need you guys!

276
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:58,920
I'll do anything please let me
join the crew just one more time?

277
00:16:16,640 --> 00:16:19,000
Hurry up!

278
00:16:19,340 --> 00:16:21,040
Grab on already!

279
00:16:33,880 --> 00:16:35,620
You better not drop them.

280
00:16:38,320 --> 00:16:40,700
Pretty lame, you two. Pull it together.

281
00:16:51,460 --> 00:16:53,800
All right, the gang's all here.

282
00:16:54,180 --> 00:16:58,217
We're going to get away from these stupid
cannonballs and head to the new world.

283
00:16:58,300 --> 00:16:59,130
Let's go.

284
00:17:09,800 --> 00:17:11,120
You can do it!

285
00:17:11,220 --> 00:17:12,537
Show the Navy who's boss!

286
00:17:12,620 --> 00:17:13,450
Are you kidding?

287
00:17:13,533 --> 00:17:14,520
They're done for!

288
00:17:14,840 --> 00:17:15,857
They're criminals.

289
00:17:15,940 --> 00:17:17,116
Don't cheer so loud.

290
00:17:17,440 --> 00:17:18,680
Come on, Straw Hat!

291
00:17:18,800 --> 00:17:19,859
Don't give up now!

292
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,400
Keep moving!

293
00:17:21,680 --> 00:17:22,980
Go, go, go!

294
00:17:23,200 --> 00:17:25,020
Hang in there, big room!

295
00:17:35,380 --> 00:17:38,877
no way what the heck do they
think they're doing why are they

296
00:17:38,960 --> 00:17:44,857
burling their sails they're not
giving up are they not on your life

297
00:17:44,940 --> 00:17:50,497
i don't know what that fool is up
to but my grandson's no quitter

298
00:17:50,580 --> 00:17:55,960
i'll tell you that hurry up i
said furl the sails yeah he said

299
00:17:56,940 --> 00:18:01,277
you sure about this Franky doesn't seem
very smart to me Hey, stop being an idiot!

300
00:18:01,360 --> 00:18:03,301
Have some faith in your own ship!

301
00:18:03,660 --> 00:18:04,542
Come on, idiot!

302
00:18:04,980 --> 00:18:06,560
Come on, man!

303
00:18:07,640 --> 00:18:10,617
Just a second ago, you were
crying, and now you're...

304
00:18:10,700 --> 00:18:12,137
Nope, never mind, whatever.

305
00:18:12,220 --> 00:18:14,220
Why don't you shut up and help me?

306
00:18:14,840 --> 00:18:15,670
Don't you know?

307
00:18:15,753 --> 00:18:18,037
We can't leave until we
give this ship a name.

308
00:18:18,120 --> 00:18:18,950
A name?

309
00:18:19,033 --> 00:18:20,116
At a time like this?

310
00:18:20,700 --> 00:18:21,530
Of course.

311
00:18:21,613 --> 00:18:25,199
This is our maiden voyage, so there's
no point if we don't do it now.

312
00:18:27,640 --> 00:18:30,097
Whatever it is, it's got
to have Lion in it, right?

313
00:18:30,180 --> 00:18:31,057
Wait, I got it!

314
00:18:31,140 --> 00:18:32,997
I just thought of the perfect name!

315
00:18:33,080 --> 00:18:35,397
The Black Bear, Polar Bear, Lion, Tiger!

316
00:18:35,480 --> 00:18:37,077
That's a horrible name for a ship!

317
00:18:37,160 --> 00:18:37,990
No way!

318
00:18:38,073 --> 00:18:40,237
Then how about the Super
Wolf, Gorilla Bear?

319
00:18:40,320 --> 00:18:41,150
Naming off animals.

320
00:18:41,233 --> 00:18:42,837
Can't you pick one and work from there?

321
00:18:42,920 --> 00:18:44,717
The Squid, Octopus, Chimpanzee!

322
00:18:44,800 --> 00:18:45,737
What happened to the lion?

323
00:18:45,820 --> 00:18:46,650
Uh-huh.

324
00:18:46,733 --> 00:18:49,077
Well, I did have a lion
in mind for the design.

325
00:18:49,160 --> 00:18:52,160
Though the guys at Galilad
didn't seem to get that.

326
00:18:52,440 --> 00:18:54,880
That figurehead's nice, huh? Yeah!

327
00:18:55,060 --> 00:18:56,580
I love sunflowers!

328
00:18:56,720 --> 00:18:58,457
I'm a sunflower, you morons!

329
00:18:58,540 --> 00:19:00,300
Well, don't take it so hard.

330
00:19:00,540 --> 00:19:03,297
You can't expect that everyone is
going to see it for what it is.

331
00:19:03,380 --> 00:19:06,397
But this is the ship the future
king of the pirates will ride.

332
00:19:06,480 --> 00:19:08,877
That's what you were thinking
when you built it, right, Franky?

333
00:19:08,960 --> 00:19:09,790
Damn straight.

334
00:19:09,900 --> 00:19:11,917
The oceans in the new
world may have monsters,

335
00:19:12,000 --> 00:19:14,677
but this is the king of beasts
that will reign over them all.

336
00:19:14,760 --> 00:19:16,237
A splendid sun and dis...

337
00:19:16,320 --> 00:19:17,937
It's not the sun, you moron!

338
00:19:18,020 --> 00:19:21,637
A ship as bright as the sun,
sailing with a shining smile?

339
00:19:21,720 --> 00:19:24,544
as it soars over the
dangers of a thousand seas.

340
00:19:24,720 --> 00:19:26,377
It needs a name to match that feeling.

341
00:19:26,460 --> 00:19:28,837
I told you it's not
the sun ice for brains!

342
00:19:28,920 --> 00:19:31,861
It might not be my place,
but I have a suggestion.

343
00:19:33,460 --> 00:19:35,440
Why don't you call this ship...

344
00:19:37,380 --> 00:19:38,880
The Thousand Sunny!

345
00:19:39,440 --> 00:19:40,477
Ooh, I like it!

346
00:19:40,560 --> 00:19:41,972
Me too, it's super cold!

347
00:19:42,080 --> 00:19:46,257
I was thinking Dandelion, Lion, Dandy,
Unbearable Bear, but this is way better!

348
00:19:46,340 --> 00:19:47,170
Just stop!

349
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:51,654
I kind of wanted Big Boss Lionel, but
Thousand Sunny is pretty good, too.

350
00:19:51,740 --> 00:19:54,257
I was going to suggest
Creature of Darkness.

351
00:19:54,340 --> 00:19:56,377
I like Monsieur Sunflower, Purcell.

352
00:19:56,460 --> 00:19:58,342
Have all of you lost your minds?

353
00:19:58,960 --> 00:20:02,000
A ship to sail a thousand
seas with a sunny smile.

354
00:20:02,480 --> 00:20:04,245
It's perfect, don't you think?

355
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,237
Don't get too excited, you guys.

356
00:20:06,320 --> 00:20:07,497
That was just a warm-up.

357
00:20:07,580 --> 00:20:10,057
I've got a name that's
gonna knock your socks off.

358
00:20:10,140 --> 00:20:12,277
This ship will now be known as...

359
00:20:12,360 --> 00:20:14,277
Hello, guys, Pop's idea just fine.

360
00:20:14,360 --> 00:20:15,997
Let's go with that and get this ship done.

361
00:20:16,080 --> 00:20:16,910
Sounds good.

362
00:20:16,993 --> 00:20:18,111
A thousandth sunny it is.

363
00:20:18,700 --> 00:20:19,530
I agree!

364
00:20:19,613 --> 00:20:20,443
Nice to meet you, Sunny!

365
00:20:20,526 --> 00:20:24,137
Thought we'd have a harder time agreeing
on this, but I guess it worked out fine.

366
00:20:24,220 --> 00:20:25,050
So it did.

367
00:20:27,000 --> 00:20:29,471
Hey, Franky, stop pouting and get moving.

368
00:20:29,980 --> 00:20:32,897
Use this secret weapon of yours
so we can get out of here.

369
00:20:32,980 --> 00:20:34,417
Better make it fast, too.

370
00:20:34,500 --> 00:20:36,417
The Navy's gonna catch up any second.

371
00:20:36,500 --> 00:20:37,700
Yeah, yeah, I know.

372
00:20:38,100 --> 00:20:40,040
Take one last look at Water 7,

373
00:20:40,160 --> 00:20:42,317
because it's gonna be out
of sight before you know it.

374
00:20:42,400 --> 00:20:46,047
I'm warning you, once we start
moving, we'll really be moving.

375
00:20:46,240 --> 00:20:48,100
Okay, got it. One sec.

376
00:20:49,960 --> 00:20:50,790
Grandpa!

377
00:20:53,160 --> 00:20:56,100
Oh, and if you're there, Colby, and...

378
00:20:57,880 --> 00:20:59,100
The other guy!

379
00:20:59,320 --> 00:21:01,026
It was nice to see you again!

380
00:21:01,620 --> 00:21:03,597
You forgot my name again, didn't you?

381
00:21:03,680 --> 00:21:05,577
What are you yapping about, Luffy?

382
00:21:05,660 --> 00:21:07,500
I got plenty more cannonballs.

383
00:21:09,180 --> 00:21:10,440
Meteor... Fish!

384
00:21:15,100 --> 00:21:16,180
Give it off!

385
00:21:17,460 --> 00:21:21,284
I don't know what's going to
happen, but we're going to get away.

386
00:21:21,480 --> 00:21:24,009
Well, I hope to see
you guys again someday.

387
00:21:24,240 --> 00:21:26,097
Wow, Loopy, that was super cool.

388
00:21:26,180 --> 00:21:29,997
You little turd, you show your
grandpa some respect, you hear me?

389
00:21:30,080 --> 00:21:31,300
How dare you?

390
00:21:31,580 --> 00:21:34,077
I know he's annoying you
like that, but calm down.

391
00:21:34,160 --> 00:21:36,807
Thanks for helping us
name the ship Ice Pops.

392
00:21:36,940 --> 00:21:37,822
You're awesome.

393
00:21:38,320 --> 00:21:40,460
And thanks to everybody else, too.

394
00:21:41,040 --> 00:21:42,540
Bye, Monster Granny.

395
00:21:42,900 --> 00:21:44,100
Bye, Galley-La.

396
00:21:44,500 --> 00:21:45,920
We had a great time.

397
00:21:46,180 --> 00:21:47,945
I think he's saying something.

398
00:21:49,360 --> 00:21:51,480
I can't hear a darn thing.

399
00:21:51,820 --> 00:21:56,057
It seems that pirates can't even go out
to sea without causing a giant ruckus.

400
00:21:56,140 --> 00:21:57,200
There we go.

401
00:21:57,720 --> 00:22:01,837
Combining the power of our air can
with the durability of the Atomwood,

402
00:22:01,920 --> 00:22:04,449
I've made an emergency
acceleration device.

403
00:22:04,560 --> 00:22:06,700
I'll pound some manners into you.

404
00:22:08,640 --> 00:22:10,180
Luffy, run away!

405
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:13,360
He's serious this time!

406
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:14,710
Breaking!

407
00:22:17,180 --> 00:22:19,180
There it goes!

408
00:22:25,920 --> 00:22:28,300
We're all gonna die!

409
00:22:29,140 --> 00:22:32,020
Who did first?

410
00:22:44,920 --> 00:22:49,140
Did their ship take off and fly away?

411
00:22:58,560 --> 00:23:00,280
Not bad, kiddo.

412
00:23:09,940 --> 00:23:11,240
I can't believe it.

413
00:23:11,360 --> 00:23:14,360
I never thought I'd feel
this again, but here I am.

414
00:23:18,100 --> 00:23:18,930
Mary.

415
00:23:19,540 --> 00:23:23,457
It eats up three barrels of cola,
but it can fly for a whole kilometer.

416
00:23:23,540 --> 00:23:25,857
I'm not trying to brag
here, but simply put,

417
00:23:25,940 --> 00:23:28,637
anything that Going Mary could
do, this ship can do better.

418
00:23:28,720 --> 00:23:30,597
And it's got tricks of its own.

419
00:23:30,680 --> 00:23:32,357
But even if it's all new!

420
00:23:32,440 --> 00:23:36,146
I hope the brave spirit of the
Mary can live on in this sudden?

421
00:23:36,440 --> 00:23:39,197
If anything breaks, I'll
fix it up as good as new.

422
00:23:39,280 --> 00:23:42,557
From weapons to furniture, I
know this ship up and down.

423
00:23:42,640 --> 00:23:46,080
It may be my masterpiece,
but it's all yours now.

424
00:23:56,020 --> 00:23:57,200
I'll be damned!

425
00:23:58,280 --> 00:24:00,140
They got away after all.

426
00:24:04,520 --> 00:24:06,340
That's my grandson for you.

427
00:24:16,840 --> 00:24:19,697
It's kind of a shame I wish the
little guy had stayed with us.

428
00:24:19,780 --> 00:24:21,251
Yeah, I'm gonna miss him,

429
00:24:21,520 --> 00:24:24,277
but wherever he goes he still
wants to come to Elbeth someday.

430
00:24:24,360 --> 00:24:26,317
And we'll be there waiting when he does.

431
00:24:26,400 --> 00:24:27,520
Sounds like fun.

432
00:24:27,680 --> 00:24:31,974
We got a couple hundred years left on
us, so we can afford to be patient.

433
00:24:32,400 --> 00:24:34,097
Nothing like a job well done.

434
00:24:34,180 --> 00:24:35,300
Yeah, you said it.

435
00:24:35,500 --> 00:24:37,157
Let's see what they need at the workshop.

436
00:24:37,240 --> 00:24:39,037
We've still got repair work to do, too.

437
00:24:39,120 --> 00:24:39,950
Bring it on.

438
00:24:44,520 --> 00:24:46,402
Better head back to the station.

439
00:24:46,500 --> 00:24:48,382
Gonna be business as usual soon.

440
00:24:48,720 --> 00:24:49,840
Huh? Let's see.

441
00:24:50,060 --> 00:24:52,540
How did Big Bro do this stuff? Beats me.

442
00:24:53,040 --> 00:24:54,257
Yeah, this is bad.

443
00:24:54,340 --> 00:24:56,693
I always just did what he told me to do.

444
00:24:56,940 --> 00:24:59,297
Guess we're going to starve to death, huh?

445
00:24:59,380 --> 00:25:00,210
Iceberg!

446
00:25:00,360 --> 00:25:03,177
I had a feeling something like this
would happen to you, Riff Reef.

447
00:25:03,260 --> 00:25:04,090
What?

448
00:25:04,173 --> 00:25:05,997
Did you come here just to make fun of us?

449
00:25:06,080 --> 00:25:07,900
No, I came to offer you a job.

450
00:25:08,160 --> 00:25:11,807
If you need work, then you should
stop by the Galley-La offices.

451
00:25:12,120 --> 00:25:13,257
Do you really mean it, Iceberg?

452
00:25:13,340 --> 00:25:14,840
Icebro? No! Bigbro!

453
00:25:15,240 --> 00:25:16,680
Our new Bigbro!

454
00:25:17,200 --> 00:25:18,030
Stop that.

455
00:25:23,980 --> 00:25:29,720
Commodore Smoker, excellent work Huh, you
said that pirate had a 50 million bounty?

456
00:25:29,940 --> 00:25:30,770
Yes, sir.

457
00:25:31,000 --> 00:25:33,897
Pathetic, the Navy standards
are dropping these days!

458
00:25:33,980 --> 00:25:36,437
One disappointment after another.

459
00:25:36,520 --> 00:25:37,837
Excuse me, Smoker.

460
00:25:37,920 --> 00:25:38,750
It's in Tashigi.

461
00:25:38,833 --> 00:25:41,320
Did you see the Straw Hats wanted posters?

462
00:25:41,600 --> 00:25:45,012
They all have bounties Who do
you think you're talking to?

463
00:25:45,380 --> 00:25:48,980
Oh, you're not Smoker, oops
Wear your glasses, stupid.

464
00:25:52,600 --> 00:25:53,430
Unbelievable!

465
00:25:54,060 --> 00:25:58,580
Nico, Robin, what in the world is
Miss Allsunday doing on Luffy's crew?

466
00:25:59,220 --> 00:26:03,497
I knew there was something mysterious about
that woman, but this is quite the shock.

467
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:05,660
If this news reaches Princess Vivi,

468
00:26:05,760 --> 00:26:08,642
I can only imagine how
disheartened she would be.

469
00:26:08,800 --> 00:26:09,737
Oh, don't worry.

470
00:26:09,820 --> 00:26:11,197
I already heard about that.

471
00:26:11,280 --> 00:26:12,337
It's no big deal, though.

472
00:26:12,420 --> 00:26:13,596
It's not a big deal!

473
00:26:13,740 --> 00:26:16,387
I thought you of all
people would be shocked!

474
00:26:17,220 --> 00:26:19,297
Even when you're as
close to Luffy as I was,

475
00:26:19,380 --> 00:26:21,968
you can never quite
tell what he's thinking.

476
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:26,925
Whether I understand his reasoning or not,
I still believe in everything he does.

477
00:26:27,300 --> 00:26:31,097
Because I know that he's going to
be king of the pirates one day.

478
00:26:31,180 --> 00:26:33,737
The best we can do is
respect his decisions.

479
00:26:33,820 --> 00:26:35,020
How forgiving.

480
00:26:35,400 --> 00:26:38,780
You've turned into such a fine
young lady, Princess Vivi.

481
00:26:39,360 --> 00:26:42,060
Hey, it's nothing to cry about. Out.

482
00:26:46,760 --> 00:26:51,297
The navy will always be the navy and
as long as we're part of the military

483
00:26:51,380 --> 00:26:55,277
there's a limit to what we can
accomplish on our own in other words

484
00:26:55,360 --> 00:26:59,397
what we need is a higher rank after
that incident at Enies Lobby pirates

485
00:26:59,480 --> 00:27:03,437
from all over the world will be
looking up to Straw Hat and his crew

486
00:27:03,520 --> 00:27:04,350
i see

487
00:27:06,680 --> 00:27:11,580
i'm putting my pride on the line here i
swear i will crush them in the new world

488
00:27:16,440 --> 00:27:18,080
All right, guys!

489
00:27:20,680 --> 00:27:21,760
Are you ready?

490
00:27:22,300 --> 00:27:23,130
Yeah!

491
00:27:23,600 --> 00:27:28,560
Then everybody raise a glass for the
return of our old friends Robin and Usopp,

492
00:27:28,820 --> 00:27:31,173
as well as our new crew member, Franky?

493
00:27:31,260 --> 00:27:34,180
and the best ship ever,
the Thousand Money!

494
00:27:34,520 --> 00:27:36,108
Let's hear it for our crew!

495
00:27:36,760 --> 00:27:37,590
Cheers!

496
00:27:47,100 --> 00:27:48,600
Let's go!

497
00:27:48,900 --> 00:27:50,780
Next stop, Fishman Island!

498
00:27:51,400 --> 00:27:52,230
Yeah!
